      "ref": "TMM/Part22/16/16/3",
      "quote": "If a trade mark consists of a surname combined with words that are considered to be descriptive in relation to the particular goods and / or services it is unlikely that it will be sufficiently inherently adapted to distinguish."
    },
    {
      "ref": "TMM/Part22/16/16/3",
      "quote": "The mark as-a-whole would not be prima facie capable of distinguishing the applicant’s services from those of other traders."
